{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Abraham was old, and YHWH had blessed.</b> It explains the circumstances that compelled Abraham to send his servant to another land for a wife for his son, and that he needed to make him swear an oath concerning this: for because of his old age he feared he might die and not see his son's wedding, and he resolved not to delay any longer. And since there was no suitable woman for his son in his own land, he needed to send to another land. And because of his wealth he feared that some unsuitable man might offer his servant abundant bribes so that he would choose that man's daughter, and would not strive to obtain a suitable wife for his son. Therefore he needed to make his servant swear an oath concerning all these matters."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:17.770392291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}